{"repositoryId":1409040885,"availability":"available","full":"8haol/selah","name":"selah","description":"Worship slides for Chinese-speaking churches: per-character pinyin layout engine, PPTX export, sheet-music recognition","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T15:57:09Z","updated":"2026-10-12T08:02:18Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://selah-8haol.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://selah-8haol.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:04.763Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:04.763Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:04.763Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T11:46:04.763Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Worship slides for Chinese-speaking churches. Type or photograph a song's lyrics, pick an arrangement (V1 C V2 C B C) and a theme, and download a PowerPoint deck. Every Chinese character in the deck has its pinyin aligned above it, and the type is sized to stay readable from the back row.","Selah (סֶלָה): the word in the Psalms that tells the musicians to pause and lift.","Selah was built for a Mandarin-speaking congregation in London, where lyric slides were made by hand in PowerPoint to a fixed template: pinyin over every character (Arial 35), Chinese in a heavy sans (45), and readable contrast on the projector. Selah encodes that template once. Songs live in a shared library, and a setlist is regenerated in one click when the arrangement changes."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/8haol/selah/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"59ce9be42fa47fe2e589d873e10337760d925d2c1e19d41415dc7cc7bed2d15c","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:04.863Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:46:04.863Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Worship slides for Chinese-speaking churches. Type or photograph a song's lyrics, pick an arrangement (V1 C V2 C B C) and a theme, and download a Pow